senses.gloss:
Bahuputraka, (nt.; cf. prec.; = Pali Bahuputta, see below),
(1) n. of another caitya (cetiya) near Rājagṛha: Mv 〔iii.50.19〕; in Pali (same story) SN 〔ii.220.6〕 called Bahuputta cetiya, and located between Rājagaha and Nāḷanda; correct DPPN on this point;
(2) = prec., so read in Divy 〔201.14〕.
